! COMPARE FIELD (KF), the VFL form (code abc110001).  Reference Manual
! printed p.65:
!
!   "A field in the accumulator is algebraically compared with the
!   addressed operand.  THIS ACCUMULATOR FIELD IS THE SAME LENGTH IN
!   BYTES AS THE FIELD FROM STORAGE EXCLUSIVE OF THE SIGN BYTE, and
!   its location is specified by the offset in the usual manner.  THE
!   ACTUAL ACCUMULATOR SIGN IS NOT USED BY THE OPERATION.  A POSITIVE
!   SIGN IS ASSUMED FOR THE ACCUMULATOR FIELD.  The sign of the
!   storage field is used as modified by the sign modifiers.  The
!   comparison result indicators are set to describe the accumulator
!   field as compared with the storage field.  Neither operand is
!   changed by the operation.  The arithmetic result indicators are
!   not affected."
!
! and the programming note on the same page, which is the whole
! difference from COMPARE:
!
!   "The field comparison operations are the only arithmetic
!   operations that do not treat the entire accumulator contents as a
!   single quantity.  Comparisons are made between fields of equal
!   length in numeric bytes.  For this reason, NO INDICATION IS GIVEN
!   in these operations IF THERE IS A ONE-BIT IN THE ACCUMULATOR TO
!   THE LEFT OF THE FIELD which is being compared with the storage
!   operand."
!
! So K takes everything left of the offset WITH ITS REAL SIGN; KF
! takes a bounded field with a FORCED POSITIVE sign and ignores
! whatever sits above it.  Blocks 4 and 5 are the two halves of that
! sentence and are the reason this deck exists: under COMPARE's
! reading they would report AH and AL respectively, and under COMPARE
! FIELD's they both report AE.
!
! ARRIVED VIA MCP, printed p.17 line 30: "KF(BU,48),X IOCD" -- the
! compare that decides whether a card image IS an IOCD card, and so
! one of the two operations standing between MCP and knowing what
! devices it has (docs/boot_plan.md A2).  The 48-bit unsigned shape
! of blocks 1-5 is MCP's own.
!
! HOW EACH BLOCK REPORTS.  Z,$IND clears the indicator register
! (bits 20-63), the operand is loaded, the KF runs, and the register
! is then loaded and stored WHOLE.  Storing the register rather than
! branching on one bit of it is deliberate: a stray data flag, a
! second comparison bit or MOP left on all fail the check by making
! the number different.
!
! WHICH MEANS EVERY BLOCK ALSO WITNESSES A CLAUSE I DID NOT SET OUT
! TO TEST.  The expected values are not the bare comparison bit,
! because the LOAD that sets each block's accumulator leaves its own
! arithmetic result indicator standing, and p.65 says KF must not
! disturb it: "The arithmetic result indicators are NOT AFFECTED."
! The first run of this deck expected the bare bit and reported six
! failures whose every extra bit turned out to be that clause being
! honoured.  IBM bit values in a 64-bit word:
!
!     RLZ = 0x80   RZ = 0x40   RGZ = 0x20   RN = 0x10
!     AL  = 0x08   AE = 0x04   AH = 0x02
!
! so 0x24 is "the LOAD said result-greater-than-zero and the KF said
! accumulator-equal", and 0x94 is "the LOAD said negative and less
! than zero, and the KF said equal anyway" -- which is block 5's
! whole point stated twice over.
!
!   T1  equal, MCP's own shape.              RGZ+AE      = 0x24
!   T2  accumulator field lower.             RGZ+AL      = 0x28
!   T3  accumulator field higher.            RGZ+AH      = 0x22
!   T4  **a one-bit above the field is ignored.**        = 0x24
!       Same as T1 with accumulator bit 48 set.  K would say AH.
!   T5  **the real accumulator sign is not used.**
!       The accumulator is loaded NEGATIVE with the same magnitude,
!       so the LOAD leaves RLZ and RN standing and the KF still
!       reports equal.  K would say AL.      RLZ+RN+AE   = 0x94
!   T6  a SIGNED storage field, so the accumulator field is the
!       storage length MINUS the sign byte: (B,56,8) gives 48 bits
!       against a 48-bit accumulator field.  Positive 100 against
!       negative 100 is higher.              RGZ+AH      = 0x22

! ONE INJECTION, MEASURED, and it lands on exactly the two blocks
! written for it: KF routed through COMPARE's path instead of its own
! (the whole accumulator, with its real sign) gives T4 = 0x22, the
! bit above the field counted as making the accumulator higher, and
! T5 = 0x98, RLZ+RN+AL, the negative accumulator counted as lower.
! T1, T2, T3 and T6 do not move, because at offset 0 with no high
! bits and a positive accumulator the two operations agree -- which
! is also why nothing in the suite would have caught KF being wrong
! in those four shapes.

        SLC, (8)2000.0

! -- 1. equal ---------------------------------------------------
START   Z, $IND
        L(BU,64,8), ACC1, 0
        KF(BU,48), F1+.16, 0
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), T1, 0

! -- 2. accumulator lower ---------------------------------------
        Z, $IND
        L(BU,64,8), ACC2, 0
        KF(BU,48), F1+.16, 0
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), T2, 0

! -- 3. accumulator higher --------------------------------------
        Z, $IND
        L(BU,64,8), ACC3, 0
        KF(BU,48), F1+.16, 0
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), T3, 0

! -- 4. a one-bit above the field is ignored --------------------
        Z, $IND
        L(BU,64,8), ACC4, 0
        KF(BU,48), F1+.16, 0
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), T4, 0

! -- 5. the real accumulator sign is not used -------------------
        Z, $IND
        L(B,56,8), NEG1+.8, 0
        KF(BU,48), F1+.16, 0
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), T5, 0

! -- 6. a signed storage field: length minus the sign byte ------
        Z, $IND
        L(BU,64,8), ACC6, 0
        KF(B,56,8), FS+.8, 0
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), T6, 0

PASS    BEW, $

! Data, word-aligned: BEW is a half word, so without this every 64-bit
! field below would straddle two words and be refused.
        SLC, (8)2060.0

! The 48-bit comparand, 0x123456789ABC, as the low 48 bits of a word.
F1      DD(BU,64,8), (8)443212636115274
ACC1    DD(BU,64,8), (8)443212636115274
ACC2    DD(BU,64,8), (8)443212636115273
ACC3    DD(BU,64,8), (8)443212636115275
! The same value with accumulator bit 48 also set: KF must not see it.
ACC4    DD(BU,64,8), (8)10443212636115274
! -0x123456789ABC as a signed 56-bit field, byte size 8, sitting at
! bits 8-63 of the word: (V<<8) | (1<<7).
NEG1    DD(BU,64,8), (8)221505317046536200
ACC6    DD(BU,64,8), 100
! -100 as a signed 56-bit field at bits 8-63: (100<<8) | (1<<7).
FS      DD(BU,64,8), (8)62200

T1      DD(BU,64,8), 0
T2      DD(BU,64,8), 0
T3      DD(BU,64,8), 0
T4      DD(BU,64,8), 0
T5      DD(BU,64,8), 0
T6      DD(BU,64,8), 0

        END, START
